'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 7''' was the seventh weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on August 5, 2026 at the Aizawa Dome in [[Aizawa, Aizawa|Aizawa]], [[Aizawa Prefecture]]. The event was the final [[NOPW Wednesday]] show before the [[Island Invasion Tour]] and the seventh consecutive Wednesday night event in a different city, following [[Nagayama]] (Episode 1), [[Kurosaki]] (Episode 2), [[Tosa]] (Episode 3), [[Naruto, Naruto|Naruto]] (Episode 4), [[Anjo-Saikawa]] (Episode 5), and [[Ogasawara, Ogasawara|Ogasawara]] (Episode 6). The show served as the go-home event before the annual [[Island Invasion Tour]], with the promotion set to fly to [[Fangatapu]], [[Vaiahi Islands]], four days later. The show featured seven matches and one main-event segment, headlined by a chaotic non-finish between [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]] and [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]] after the [[Cannon Club]] turned on Vance, followed by an attack from [[Jusuf Muntasir]] and a staredown from [[Leoni Masua]], who watched the betrayal from the ramp in a conundrum.

== Background ==

Following [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 6]] on July 29 in [[Ogasawara, Ogasawara|Ogasawara]] — where the four former members of [[Kuroshio (stable)|Kuroshio]] brawled and officially ended the Black Tide bond, [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]] defeated [[Leoni Masua]] by countout after [[KAZUKI (wrestler)|KAZUKI]] interference, and [[Jusuf Muntasir]] made his shocking debut by interrupting the IGO Intercontinental Championship match — NOPW returned to the mainland for the go-home stop in [[Aizawa, Aizawa|Aizawa]], the city where Leoni had trained as a teenager and where the Vaiahi diaspora community is centred. The Aizawa Dome (capacity 10,500) sold out in 11 hours, breaking the 14-hour record set by Ogasawara the previous week. The seven consecutive sellouts across seven different markets confirmed NOPW Wednesday as the fastest-growing touring product in the company.

Key storylines entering Episode 7:
* The Kuroshio bond was dead. Leoni, [[Ryohei Maeda]], KAZUKI, and [[Daigo Kuroki]] had brawled in Ogasawara. With four days until Island Invasion, the question was whether any of them could coexist long enough to get to Fangatapu.
* KAZUKI had attacked both Maeda and Leoni. He was now completely isolated, focused only on the [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]]. A final confrontation with Kuroki — his former Kuroshio brother — was scheduled for Episode 7.
* [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]] had been abandoned by the [[Cannon Club]] during the Jusuf Muntasir attack at Episode 6. The crowd had begun to turn him into an organic babyface. Vance — a man who had always been cold, precise, and heelish — was now the most sympathetic champion in NOPW. His response to the Cannon Club, and to Jusuf, would define the go-home show.
* Jusuf Muntasir had declared professional wrestling a "lie" compared to Baliscan oil wrestling. He had attacked both Vance and Kuroki without choosing a side. A singles match with Vance for the Intercontinental Championship was announced for the [[Island Invasion Tour]] — not for Episode 7.
* The [[Cannon Club]] held four titles but was fracturing. Kengo's leadership was built on psychological warfare, not clean wins. Vance was drifting from the faction. The Usos were under pressure from Reyes and Kimura. Tanaka had lost a non-title match to Ono. The faction's depth was cracking. The go-home show was expected to expose the fracture publicly.
* The young guns — Ono, Yamamoto, Sato, Iwata — had scored surprise wins in Ogasawara. Their momentum was expected to continue in Aizawa.
* The tag team title match at Island Invasion — the Usos (c) vs. Diego Reyes and Haruto Kimura — had become personal after the DQ finish and post-match brawl at Episode 6. A final confrontation was scheduled.

