;Match details

* '''Match 1:''' Young guns momentum. '''Face vs. heel''' — Ono & Yamamoto (Seigigun) vs. Viggo & Nakamura (Cannon Club, Junior Tag Champions). The young lions continued their war of attrition against the Cannon Club junior division. Ono and Yamamoto worked fast and smart, isolating Viggo and keeping Nakamura on the apron. At 9:45, Ono pinned Viggo after a springboard DDT. The message: the future is coming for the Cannon Club's junior titles. '''Crowd:''' BIG POP for Ono & Yamamoto. HEAT for Viggo & Nakamura. "LET'S GO ONO" chants. MEGA POP for the finish.
* '''Match 2:''' TV title defense. '''Heel vs. face''' — Tanaka (c, Cannon Club) vs. Sato (Seigigun). Tanaka — still furious after losing to Ono at Episode 6 — took out his frustration on the young high-flyer Sato. The match was a methodical beating: Tanaka used size, power, and underhanded tactics to control the pace. Sato had a brief comeback with a missile dropkick and a rolling cradle, but Tanaka cut him off with a lariat and finished with the Bulldog Bomb at 11:30. Post-match: Tanaka grabbed the microphone and called out Ono — "You got lucky. At Fangatapu, I end you." '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Tanaka. POP for Sato's comeback. HEAT for the Bulldog Bomb. "ONO" chants after the promo.
* '''Match 3:''' Destruction continues. '''Heel vs. face''' — The Marauder vs. Iwata (Seigigun). Iwata was a step up from Morita — quicker, more technical, a better test of whether The Marauder could be outwrestled. The answer was no. The Marauder absorbed Iwata's early offense, caught him on the floor, and threw him into the guardrail. Back in the ring, the running big boot ended it at 7:20. The Marauder is now 4-0 on Wednesday nights. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for The Marauder. "WHO ARE YOU?" chants. GASPS for the guardrail throw. BIG POP for the big boot. The mystery man is becoming a force.
* '''Match 4:''' CHAOS vs. Cannon Club power. '''Face vs. heel''' — Kawada & Takagi vs. Big Stan & Diallo. A rematch from Episode 6, where Kawada and Takagi won. This time, the Cannon Club power team was desperate. The match was a war of strikes and throws. Big Stan dominated stretches with his size, but Kawada's veteran timing and Takagi's lariat turned the tide. At 12:10, Kawada pinned Diallo with a brainbuster — the same finish as the previous week. The Cannon Club's power team has now lost three consecutive tag matches. '''Crowd:''' POP for CHAOS. HEAT for the Cannon Club. "KAWADA" chants. MEGA POP for the brainbuster.
* '''Match 5:''' Tag title chaos. '''Heel vs. tweener/face''' — The Usos (c) vs. Reyes & Kimura, ended in a no contest. The final confrontation before Island Invasion. The match broke down almost immediately — Reyes and Kimura attacked the Usos before the bell, and the brawl spilled all over the arena. Chairs, guardrails, the announce table. The referee tried to regain control but eventually threw the match out at 14:20. No contest. The Usos retain, but the challengers have made it clear: they will do anything to take the titles. Officials separated all four men. The Island Invasion tag title match is now the most violent match on the card. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for the Usos. MEGA POP for Reyes & Kimura's attack. "COBRA" chants. HEAT for the no contest. The crowd wants to see them fight with no rules.
* '''Match 6:''' Kuroshio ghosts. '''Tweener vs. face''' — KAZUKI vs. Kuroki. The two former Kuroshio brothers — now on opposite sides of the Island Invasion main event — met for the first time since the split. Kuroki tried to reach KAZUKI, to remind him of the bond. KAZUKI responded with violence. The match was stiff and emotional, with Kuroki's strong style against KAZUKI's aerial offense. Kuroki kicked out of the Twin Star Press at 2.5, but a second one at 16:45 ended it. KAZUKI defeated his former brother. Post-match: KAZUKI stood over Kuroki, then pointed to the ramp — the message was for Leoni. '''Crowd:''' MEGA POP for both entrances. "KUROSHIO" chants — now mournful. GASPS at the first Twin Star Press kick-out. MEGA POP for the finish. Silence after.
* '''Match 7:''' Strong Openweight title match. '''Face vs. heel''' — Taumafa (c, Independent) vs. Malo (Cannon Club). The Vaiahi family war continued. Malo — sent by Kengo again — targeted Taumafa's lower back and used every underhanded tactic he could find. Taumafa fought through the pain, hitting the Samoan Spike at 15:40 to retain. Post-match: Taumafa took the microphone and challenged Kengo directly — "No more brothers. No more proxies. You and me, Fangatapu." Kengo, watching from the ramp, did not answer. '''Crowd:''' MEGA POP for Taumafa. NUCLEAR HEAT for Malo. "TAUMAFA" chants. BIG POP for the Samoan Spike. Taumafa's challenge drew a mixed reaction — the crowd wants Kengo in the ring.
* '''Match 8:''' Main event. '''Face vs. heel''' — Marcus Vance vs. Kengo Vaiahi. The match the entire night had been building toward. Vance — the Intercontinental Champion — demanded answers from the Cannon Club leader. Kengo — who had left Vance to be attacked by Jusuf at Episode 6 — accepted the match with a smile. The action was tense but short. At 8:30, Vance had Kengo locked in the Drill Driver when the rest of the Cannon Club — Malo, the Usos, Big Stan, Diallo, Tanaka, Viggo, and Nakamura — stormed the ring and attacked Vance. The referee called for the bell — no contest. Kengo stood over Vance, laughing, and took the microphone: ''"You thought you were one of us. You were never one of us. You were a tool. And now that you're broken, we throw you away."'' — NUCLEAR HEAT. The Cannon Club continued the assault. The crowd booed loudly — but then began to chant for someone, anyone, to help Vance. Leoni Masua's music hit. The Tribal Chief walked to the ring, namo in hand, and stood on the apron — watching. He looked at Vance, then at Kengo, then at the ramp. The crowd fell silent. Leoni did not enter the ring. He stepped back down and walked up the ramp, leaving Vance to the Cannon Club. Then Jusuf Muntasir's music — or rather, the sound of a single drum — hit. Jusuf walked to the ring, slid inside, and attacked Vance alongside the Cannon Club. Kengo stepped aside, amused. The show ended with Vance being beaten by his former faction and the Baliscan invader. '''Crowd:''' MIXED-to-POSITIVE reaction for Vance's entrance — the babyface turn is real. HEAT for Kengo. "VANCE" chants during the comeback. NUCLEAR HEAT for the Cannon Club attack. MEGA POP for Leoni's music. CONFUSION when Leoni did not enter. HEAT when Leoni walked away. NUCLEAR HEAT for Jusuf's appearance. The show ended in chaos.

== Post-match segment: The Cannon Club summit ==

After Vance was pulled from the ring by officials, Kengo stood in the centre of the Aizawa Dome with the Cannon Club behind him. He had a microphone.

:''"Marcus Vance thought he was the best champion in this company. He thought he was above the Cannon Club. He thought the crowd's cheers meant something."'' — HEAT

:''"The Cannon Club does not need cheerleaders. The Cannon Club does not need popular champions. The Cannon Club needs soldiers. And Marcus Vance — you are no longer a soldier."'' — NUCLEAR HEAT

:''"At Fangatapu, your title belongs to us. Your name belongs to us. And your little Baliscan problem? He belongs to us too."''

Kengo looked down at the mat. The [[IGO Intercontinental Championship]] — knocked loose during the beatdown — lay at his feet. He picked it up. Turned it over in his hands. The plate caught the arena lights. Then he walked to where Vance lay, dropped the belt on Vance's chest, and leaned in close: ''"You can keep the belt. You just can't keep us."'' — NUCLEAR HEAT. Kengo stood, smiled, and backed up the ramp. The Cannon Club posed in the ring — without Vance. The image was clear: the faction had excommunicated its most talented champion.

== Leoni's conundrum ==

In a backstage segment after the main event, Leoni Masua sat alone in his locker room. His arms were crossed. He did not look at the camera.

:''"Marcus Vance is not my friend. He is not my brother. He is a man who chose to stand with Kengo. And Kengo is a man who wants to take everything from me."'' — Pause. — ''"But tonight, Kengo threw one of his own into the fire. And the man who came to take my title watched it happen."''

:''"I could have helped Vance. Part of me wanted to. But if I help Vance, I help a Cannon Club man. If I let him burn, I let Kengo win. And if I fight Jusuf, I fight a man who is not my enemy — yet."''

:''"Fangatapu. The Chief walks in with the namo. The Chief walks out with the namo. Everything else... I will figure out when I have to."''

The segment ended with Leoni staring at the namo. The implication: the Tribal Chief sees the battlefield shifting beneath him, and he is not sure who his allies are anymore.

