== Storyline notes ==

* '''The Cannon Club excommunicates Marcus Vance.''' The main event was designed to expose Vance's isolation. When Kengo and the entire Cannon Club attacked Vance during the match, the betrayal became public and absolute. Kengo's promo — "You were never one of us" — established the leader betrayal arc: Vance, the most talented champion in the faction, is now its primary target. The storyline sets up a potential Vance vs. the entire Cannon Club feud after Island Invasion, with Vance as a lone babyface against the faction that created him.
* '''Marcus Vance vs. Jusuf Muntasir is held for Island Invasion.''' Jusuf did not wrestle at Episode 7. Instead, he appeared after the main event to attack the already-beaten Vance alongside the Cannon Club. The visual of Jusuf and the Cannon Club standing together over Vance — despite their supposed opposition — established that both see Vance as the common enemy. The Intercontinental Championship match at Fangatapu is now a three-way dynamic: Vance defending against Jusuf, while the Cannon Club waits to pick over the bones.
* '''Leoni Masua is in a conundrum.''' The Tribal Chief came to the ring during the main-event assault but chose not to intervene. His backstage promo explained the calculation: helping Vance means helping a former Cannon Club member; letting Vance burn means letting Kengo win; fighting Jusuf means making an enemy of a man who is not yet his enemy. Leoni's hesitation humanizes the champion and sets up the possibility that he may eventually align with Vance against common threats — or that his refusal to choose will cost him.
* '''KAZUKI's path of destruction.''' KAZUKI defeated Daigo Kuroki, his second consecutive victory over a former Kuroshio member after beating Ryohei Maeda at Episode 6. He has now defeated both of Leoni's former brothers. The message to Leoni: there is no one left to save you. KAZUKI's isolation is absolute, and his focus on the title is total.
* '''The Vaiahi family war.''' Taumafa defeated Malo in a Strong Openweight Championship rematch and challenged Kengo directly. Kengo did not answer. The family hierarchy remains unresolved, and the strong possibility of a Kengo vs. Taumafa match at Island Invasion was teased.
* '''The young guns continue their war of attrition.''' Ono and Yamamoto defeated two Junior Tag Champions. Sato pushed World TV Champion Jin Tanaka to the limit in a competitive title match. The Cannon Club's junior and mid-card depth is under serious pressure.
* '''Tag team title match becomes a street fight.''' The no contest between the Usos and Reyes & Kimura — with the pre-bell attack and arena-wide brawl — established that the Island Invasion match will be violent and personal. The Usos have retained twice by non-clean finishes, making them look vulnerable despite holding the titles.
* '''The Marauder remains undefeated.''' Four consecutive Wednesday night wins. The mysterious powerhouse is becoming a problem that NOPW will have to address after Island Invasion.
* '''The Aizawa Dome sellout.''' 10,500 tickets sold in 11 hours, breaking the Ogasawara record. The Wednesday night product has now sold out seven consecutive shows in seven different markets: Nagayama (4,200), Kurosaki (6,500), Tosa (6,000), Naruto (7,500), Okayama (8,500), Ogasawara (9,000), and Aizawa (10,500). The growth is unprecedented. The next stop is Fangatapu, Vaiahi Islands — the biggest event of the NOPW calendar.

