== Aftermath ==

* The Cannon Club publicly excommunicated Marcus Vance at Episode 7. Kengo led the entire faction in an attack on Vance during the main event, then cut a promo declaring Vance was "never one of us." The betrayal sets up a leader-vs-former-soldier arc that will likely dominate the post-Island Invasion landscape. Vance enters Fangatapu as a lone babyface Intercontinental Champion, targeted by both his former faction and Jusuf Muntasir.
* Jusuf Muntasir did not wrestle at Episode 7. Instead, he appeared after the main event to attack the beaten Vance alongside the Cannon Club — a visual that suggested Jusuf and the Cannon Club share a common enemy even if they are not allies. The Intercontinental Championship match between Vance and Jusuf is now the most anticipated non-main-event match at Island Invasion.
* Leoni Masua's conundrum was the emotional centre of the show. He came to the ring during the assault on Vance but chose not to intervene, then walked away. His backstage promo explained the impossible choice: helping Vance helps a former Cannon Club member; letting Vance burn lets Kengo win; fighting Jusuf makes an unnecessary enemy. Leoni enters Island Invasion as a champion carrying not just the namo but the weight of a shifting battlefield.
* KAZUKI defeated Daigo Kuroki, his second consecutive victory over a former Kuroshio member. He has now beaten Ryohei Maeda and Daigo Kuroki, leaving Leoni with no former brothers to stand beside him. The IGO Heavyweight Championship match at Fangatapu is now a pure one-on-one contest between champion and challenger.
* Taumafa Vaiahi retained the Strong Openweight Championship against Malo and challenged Kengo directly. The Vaiahi family war remains unresolved, with a potential Kengo vs. Taumafa confrontation at Island Invasion now strongly teased.
* The tag team title match between the Usos and Reyes & Kimura ended in a no contest after a wild pre-bell brawl. The challengers have made it clear they will use any means necessary to win. The Island Invasion match is now expected to be a violent, possibly no-disqualification contest.
* The young guns continued their rise. Ono and Yamamoto defeated two Junior Tag Champions. Akira Sato pushed World TV Champion Jin Tanaka to the limit in a competitive title match. The Cannon Club's junior and mid-card depth is under serious pressure.
* The Marauder defeated Shota Iwata to move to 4-0 on Wednesday nights. The mysterious powerhouse is becoming a significant problem that NOPW will have to address after Island Invasion.
* The Aizawa Dome sellout (10,500) in 11 hours was the fastest in Wednesday night history, breaking the Ogasawara record. The product has now sold out seven consecutive shows in seven markets. The next stop is Fangatapu, Vaiahi Islands, for the biggest event of the NOPW calendar.

